    "lawCode": "Amd §4, Chap 668 of 1977",
    "lawSection": "Firefighters",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8011\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 668 of the laws of 1977, amending the volunteer\nfirefighters' benefit law relating to disability due to disease or\nmalfunction of the heart or coronary arteries, in relation to the effec-\ntiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis legislation would extend, until June 30, 2030, § 61 of the Volun-\nteer Firefighters' Benefit Law, which governs benefits for the death or\ndisability of volunteer firefighters due to heart or coronary artery\ndisease.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends § 61 of the Volunteer Firefighters Benefits Law to\nextend the presumption related to disability benefits for death or disa-\nbility due to heart or coronary artery disease for an additional five\nyears.\n\nSection two provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn 1977, the Legislature found that volunteer firefighters too often\nsuffered injuries or deaths resulting from heart attacks suffered in the\nline of duty. The Legislature also found that claims of injuries from\nheart attacks were often subjected to lengthy delays. As a result, the\nLegislature established specific procedures to expedite the handling of\nsuch claims. This legislation extends the provisions relating to disa-\nbility due to heart disease which are scheduled to expire on June 30,\n2025.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2020 - Chapter 58 of the Laws of 2020 (PPGG Part XXX subpart B item CC)\n\n2015 - Chapter 26 of the Laws of 2015\n\n2010 - Chapter 183 of the Laws of 2010\n\n2005 - Chapter 138 of the Laws 2005\n\n2003 - Chapter 89 of the Laws of 2003\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
